      "section_path_text": "Arabian Gulf Load Area",
      "level": 1,
      "ordinal": 5,
      "summary": "While it is normal to \"blame\" crude exports from the Arabian Gulf to China for high VLCC rates over the last two years, the chart on the next page shows that there have been marked growth in the number of cargo liftings to India from 51 spot fixtures in 2000 to 111 in 2004, the United States from 164 spot fixtures in 2000 to 206 in 2004, and Europe from 39 spot fixtures in 2000 to 95 in 2005, probably as compensation for falling North Sea production. The number of liftings to the Red Sea (Sumed pipeline) and to South Africa has remained fairly constant.",
